# AgentIDE remote access: the sandbox account only, keys only, so a
# forwarded port reaches agents and nothing else on this Mac.

# The account allowed in. Belt and braces with the Sharing pane's
# com.apple.access_ssh group, and the half that does not depend on a
# hidden account showing up in a menu.
AllowUsers @SANDVAULT_USER@

# Keys only. The account has a password hash, and an internet-facing
# port must never accept it.
PasswordAuthentication no

# The other road to a password prompt, which PAM still offers on
# macOS when only the line above is set.
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no

# Root has no business on this port; nothing here needs it.
PermitRootLogin no

# Three attempts per connection, so a client cannot walk a keyring
# and a scanner gets disconnected quickly.
MaxAuthTries 3

# Twenty seconds to authenticate: generous for a phone waking up,
# mean to a scanner holding connections open.
LoginGraceTime 20

# Ten unauthenticated connections at most, refused at random from
# three upwards, so a scan cannot crowd out your own login.
MaxStartups 3:50:10

# This port exists to attach terminals. No forwarding of any kind,
# so a stolen key cannot become a route into the home LAN.
AllowTcpForwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no
X11Forwarding no
PermitTunnel no

# Hang up on a client that has been silent for two minutes (three
# probes, forty seconds apart), so a phone that loses signal does not
# leave an attached Herdr client behind for ever.
ClientAliveInterval 40
ClientAliveCountMax 3

# System SSH sessions do not inherit the app's shared workspace. Match blocks
# own everything after them, so this stays last.
Match User @SANDVAULT_USER@
  SetEnv SHARED_WORKSPACE=@SANDVAULT_SHARED_WORKSPACE@
